    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nhues\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nGit highlights are excessively saturated with randomhues, which clash with the overall colorscheme due to poor contrast.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.2\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ncat <<EOF > minimal.patch\r\n-Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Aenean congue dignissim tristique.\r\n+Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Aenean congue dignissim tristique.\r\nEOF\r\n```\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.patch`\r\n2. `vim.cmd [[colorscheme randomhue]]`\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nHighlight that adhere to randomhue / mini.hues colorspace.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/de2a4064-89a8-46e9-bfab-9b7254504c59)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/ab8df6ac-46bd-47c0-a098-7dae14892292)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/6aab88a8-fda6-4729-aaab-3748cf43b73b)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/ba2f08f8-57f6-4e06-88e1-a1878413d503)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/66afc303-d4ef-48f0-98bc-6d79265c881b)\r\n\r\n",
