            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the creating this!\r\n\r\nThis is by design. The diff highlight groups [have colored backgrounds](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/66e3cdceaba8c0cd089d6f42cb95e04355718f7a/lua/mini/hues.lua#L663-L665) which [are](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/66e3cdceaba8c0cd089d6f42cb95e04355718f7a/lua/mini/hues.lua#L347) [computed](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/66e3cdceaba8c0cd089d6f42cb95e04355718f7a/lua/mini/hues.lua#L353) [to have](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/66e3cdceaba8c0cd089d6f42cb95e04355718f7a/lua/mini/hues.lua#L356) same lightness as background and same chroma as text. Having different lightness would make it stand out in a more unnatural way (subjectively) than different chroma. Having smaller chroma would make them too indistinguishable to background in most cases.\r\n\r\nWhat would be your preferred way of coloring those?",
