            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Fair enough - That said, would you be open to having an option to use either base16-style diff highlight or 'tokyonight'-ish style? This would make the transition from base16 to randomhue less jarring overall\r\n\r\nSorry, but no. Color schemes need only so much configuration and I feel that 'mini.hues' already reached its limit. The best suggestion from me here is to manually change those highlight groups (ideally, inside an autocommand for `ColorScheme` before calling `require('mini.hues').setup()`)",
            "created_at": "2023-10-24T12:34:51Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/538#issuecomment-1777119541",
